$\begin{align}
\text{vertex's }r\text{-coordinate}&=\dfrac{(\goldD{11})+(\goldD{-5})}{2}
\\\\
&=\blueD{3}
\end{align}$

Now we can find the vertex's $y$-coordinate by evaluating $g(\blueD{3})$:

$\begin{align}
g(\blueD{3})&=(\blueD{3})^2-6(\blueD{3})-55
\\\\
&=9-18-55
\\\\
&=-64
\end{align}$
